zend_try/zend_bailout with setjmp/longjmp on WASI (wasix-php).

On wasix-sysroot's asyncify tree, setjmp is a WASIX stack snapshot that has
to be taken in the calling function's frame, and <setjmp.h> declares no
sigsetjmp/siglongjmp (libc.a has wrappers, but a wrapper's frame is gone
when longjmp comes back). SETJMP/LONGJMP use setjmp/longjmp directly, as
on Windows; the signal mask was never saved (sigsetjmp(a, 0)).

--- a/Zend/zend_portability.h
+++ b/Zend/zend_portability.h
@@ -424,7 +424,9 @@
 # define XtOffsetOf(s_type, field) offsetof(s_type, field)
 #endif
 
-#ifndef ZEND_WIN32
+/* WASIX (asyncify sysroot): setjmp is a stack snapshot that must be taken in
+ * the caller's own frame, and <setjmp.h> declares no sigsetjmp there. */
+#if !defined(ZEND_WIN32) && !defined(__wasi__)
 # define SETJMP(a) sigsetjmp(a, 0)
 # define LONGJMP(a,b) siglongjmp(a, b)
 # define JMP_BUF sigjmp_buf
